# About Allen

![Allen](/img/avatar.jpg)

Allen is a native Chinese speaker who teaches Chinese to learners outside China, in clear English.

His approach is simple: start with a real scene, give you a real sentence, explain why Chinese people say it that way, and then let you practise it. Culture is not an extra chapter at the end — it is the reason the sentence sounds the way it does.

> Full introduction, teaching background, and a longer bilingual introduction will be added here. This page is intentionally short at launch, rather than filled with claims that are not yet written.

## What you will learn here

- Chinese you can actually say, not only read in a textbook
- Why a direct translation often sounds wrong, and what sounds natural instead
- Chinese culture through language: greetings, food, family, festivals, and daily life

